            "target_entity_instance": "energy spectrum",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "The metrics for verifying prognostic variables are the Root Mean Square Error (RMSE) and the energy spectrum. The energy spectrum is radially averaged, which quantifies the distribution of variance in downscaling outputs across spatial scales (Morss, Snyder, & Rotunno, 2009). It is computed using 2-D Fast Fourier Transforms with a Hann window. The focus of this evaluation is the amount of spatial variance that contributes to the 10-100 km mesoscale wavelength.",
